            <ArticleTitle>Unstable angina in a patient with mucocutaneous lymph node syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>661-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An 11-year-old boy with mucocutaneous lymph node syndrome, who later developed an acute anteroseptal infarction and unstable angina, is presented. Anginal attacks were shown by 24-hour long-term ambulatory electrocardiographic recording. He was shown to have multiple coronary aneurysms with thrombi, and underwent a successful aorto-coronary bypass.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
